! ---- Engine unit tests: ENGINETEST compares the pure coordinate transforms of
! mod_surface_placement (place_into_surface, back_to_object, forward_from_object)
! bit-for-bit against legacy TRNSF2, BAKONE and FORONEL for the current lens, over
! a fixed set of 20 rays at every surface.  It also compares legacy CACHEK (clear
! aperture / obscuration / erase check) with check_apertures, which is the
! "CACHEK: cases N, mismatches M" line; see the aperture cases from case 14 on.
! BRIEF prints counts, the integer flag summary and the verdict only (no
! floating-point values).
! Every case starts from RES osdtriplet, applies one tilt/decenter type in
! lens-update level (U L ... EOS), runs FOB 0.7, then ENGINETEST BRIEF.
!
! Flag coverage (TILT FLAGS line of each case shows the surface flags):
!   case 1   no tilts                             flag 0 (cur), decenter flag 0
!   case 2   DEC only (no tilt)                   flag 0 + decenter flag 1
!   case 3   TILT + DEC + GDX/GDY/GDZ             flag 1; global offsets (S3);
!                                                 BAKONE/FORONEL flag 1 (S1)
!   case 4   RTILT + DEC                          flag -1 (cur, BAKONE, FORONEL)
!   case 5   TILT BEN + DEC                       flag 4 (cur at S3, prev for S4)
!   case 6   TILT DAR + DEC                       flag 5 (cur, and prev for S4)
!   case 7   TILT REV + DEC                       flag 7 (cur, and prev for S4)
!   case 8   TILT AUTO                            flag 2
!   case 9   TILT AUTOM                           flag 3
!   case 10  TILT RET                             flag 6 is transient: EOS resolves
!                                                 it to 1 (+return flag), so 6 itself
!                                                 never survives to trace time.  The
!                                                 TRNSF2 test (1,6,2,3,4,5) shares
!                                                 one branch, covered by 1/2/3/4/5.
!   case 11  TILT + PIVOT + PIVAXIS NORMAL (S1)   FORONEL pivot path (flag 1)
!   case 12  RTILT + PIVOT + PIVAXIS NORMAL (S1)  FORONEL pivot path (flag -1)
!   case 13  mixed types on adjacent surfaces     prev/cur combinations:
!            (TILT, RTILT, BEN, DAR, REV, TILT)   (1,-1) (-1,4) (4,5) (5,7) (7,1)
! Not reachable from any command: TILT BEN and TILT DAR are rejected on surface
! NEWOBJ+1 ("DISALLOWED ON SURFACES 0 AND 1"), so BAKONE's flag-4 and flag-5
! branches and FORONEL's flag-4 branch and flag-5 pivot path cannot be exercised
! (they run only through BAKONE/FORONEL, which only look at surface NEWOBJ+1);
! TILT REV is likewise rejected there.  The global ANGLES (surf_global_alpha/beta/gamma) are
! never set by any live command (only GDX/GDY/GDZ are), so the global-rotation
! branches run with zero angles.
! ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

! case 1
RES osdtriplet
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 2
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 1
DEC 0.1 -0.2 0.3
CHG 3
DEC -0.3 0.2 0.1
EOS
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 3
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 1
TILT 0.5 0.3 0.2
CHG 3
TILT 1 2 3
DEC 0.1 0.2 0.3
GDX 0.4
GDY 0.5
GDZ 0.6
EOS
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 4
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 1
RTILT 0.5 0.3 0.2
DEC 0.1 -0.2 0.3
CHG 3
RTILT 1 2 3
DEC 0.3 0.2 0.1
EOS
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 5
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 3
TILT BEN 2 3
DEC 0.1 0.2 0.3
EOS
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 6
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 3
TILT DAR 2 3 1
DEC 0.1 0.2 0.3
EOS
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 7
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 3
TILT REV 2 3 1
DEC 0.1 0.2 0.3
EOS
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 8
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 5
TILT AUTO 2 3 1
EOS
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 9
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 5
TILT AUTOM 2 3 1
EOS
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 10
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 3
TILT RET 1
EOS
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 11
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 1
TILT 1 2 3
PIVOT 2 3 0
PIVAXIS NORMAL
EOS
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 12
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 1
RTILT 1 2 3
PIVOT 2 3 0
PIVAXIS NORMAL
EOS
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 13
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 1
TILT 0.5 0.3 0.2
CHG 2
RTILT 0.4 0.2 0.1
DEC 0.1 0.1 0.1
CHG 3
TILT BEN 1 2
DEC 0.2 -0.1 0.3
CHG 4
TILT DAR 0.6 0.3 0.1
DEC -0.2 0.1 0.2
CHG 5
TILT REV 0.7 0.2 0.3
DEC 0.1 0.3 -0.1
CHG 6
TILT 0.3 0.6 0.2
DEC 0.2 0.2 0.2
GDX 0.1
GDY 0.2
GDZ 0.3
EOS
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
! CACHEK / check_apertures cases (14-25).  For every surface NEWOBJ+1..NEWIMG-1
! the test runs a 41x41 grid spanning +-1.5x the largest aperture dimension, plus
! points on and within 1e-8/1e-6 (relative) of the nominal edges and corners of
! each aperture record, through legacy CACHEK and the port, from identical
! sentinel state, and requires the same RAYCOD(1:2), STOPP, /CACO/ (CAERAS,
! COERAS, LS bit for bit) and SPDCD1/2.  Modes: CACOCA 0, 1 and 2 with zero
! offsets, with arbitrary JK1/JK2/JK3 offsets and extra tilt, CACOCA 0 with
! NOCOBSPSF set, every MULTCLAP entry in mode 1 and MULTCOBS entry in mode 2 (as
! the CACOCH loop of real-ray-trace.f90 feeds them), all at AIMTOL and at 1e-3.
! Case 1-13 lenses have no apertures: they cover CACHEK's "no CLAP/COBS" early
! return.  Every ENGINETEST also runs a built-in synthetic pass on surface
! NEWOBJ+1 for shapes no script can create (see below), so its counts are part of
! every CACHEK line.
!
!   case 14  CLAP circle (CAFLG 1): decentered (S1), dim1 <= dim2 and dim1 > dim2
!            (S2, "CLAP 3 0 0 2": legacy radius = the smaller), ELIP + CLAP TILT
!            + decenter (CAFLG 3, S4)
!   case 15  CLAP RECT + tilt + decenter (CAFLG 2, S1); RCTK with radius < the
!            larger side: 8-sided box (CAFLG 4, S2, with tilt); RCTK with radius
!            = side of a square: 4-sided box (S4)
!   case 16  CLAP POLY with tilt and decenter (CAFLG 5, S1, S2)
!   case 17  COBS circle (COFLG 1, S1); COBS RECT + tilt + decenter (COFLG 2, S2);
!            COBS ELIP + tilt + decenter (COFLG 3, S4)
!   case 18  COBS RCTK 8-sided with tilt (COFLG 4, S1); COBS RCTK 4-sided (S2);
!            COBS POLY with tilt (COFLG 5, S4)
!   case 19  CLAP ERASE and COBS ERASE circular (CAERAS 1 in CAERRS, COERAS 1 in
!            COERRS), decentered
!   case 20  CLAP RECTE + CLAP TILTE, COBS RECTE + COBS TILTE (CAERAS/COERAS 2)
!   case 21  ELIPE for clap and cobs with TILTE (CAERAS/COERAS 3)
!   case 22  RCTKE for clap and cobs (CAERAS/COERAS 4): 8-sided box with side
!            1 <= side 2 (clap S1) and side 1 > side 2 (cobs S2, clap S3, the
!            two MAXSID branches), 4-sided box from a square (clap S4, cobs S5)
!   case 23  COBS POLYE with TILTE (COERAS 5)
!   case 24  FOOTBLOK YES on a surface with a CLAP (footblock early return, S1);
!            CLAP + COBS + SPIDER (S2).  CACHEK never reads the spider data (the
!            spider only affects drawing), so this case shows the spider changes
!            nothing; there is no spider field in surface_apertures.
!   case 25  MULTCLAP / MULTCOBS entries on three surfaces (JK1/JK2/JK3 from the
!            tables, as CACOCH uses them)
!
! Synthetic pass (built into ENGINETEST, restores the surface afterwards):
!   * type 6 (IPOLY) clap, clap erase, cobs and cobs erase: CAFLG/COFLG/CAERAS/
!     COERAS 6.  These shapes load their vertices from an IPOLYnn.DAT file in the
!     working directory, which no script can provide.
!   * type 5 (POLYE) clap erase: the CLAP POLYE command stores the data and then
!     always rejects it (a legacy test requires NW2 = 0 although the message says
!     3..200), aborting the lens update, so a valid polygon clap erase cannot be
!     entered from a command.
! Not reachable at all: negative shape types (the code takes ABS of the stored
! type, but every setter stores a positive value).
! ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

! case 14
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 1
CLAP 3 0.2 -0.1
CHG 2
CLAP 3 0 0 2
CHG 4
CLAP ELIP 3 2 0.2 -0.3
CLAP TILT 25
EOS
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 15
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 1
CLAP RECT 3 2 0.2 -0.1
CLAP TILT 20
CHG 2
CLAP RCTK 3 2 0 0 1
CLAP TILT -15
CHG 4
CLAP RCTK 2 2 0.1 0.1 2
EOS
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 16
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 1
CLAP POLY 3 5 0.1 -0.2
CLAP TILT 12
CHG 2
CLAP POLY 2.5 6
EOS
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 17
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 1
COBS 1.5 0.2 -0.1
CHG 2
COBS RECT 1 2 0.1 0.2
COBS TILT 30
CHG 4
COBS ELIP 2 1 -0.2 0.3
COBS TILT -20
EOS
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 18
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 1
COBS RCTK 3 2 0.1 -0.1 1
COBS TILT 10
CHG 2
COBS RCTK 2 2 0 0 2
CHG 4
COBS POLY 2.5 5 0.1 0.2
COBS TILT 18
EOS
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 19
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 1
CLAP 1.5 0 0
CLAP ERASE 3 0.1 0.2
CHG 2
COBS 2 0 0
COBS ERASE 1 0.2 0.1
EOS
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 20
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 1
CLAP 1.5 0 0
CLAP RECTE 1 3 0.1 0.2
CLAP TILTE 0.3
CHG 2
COBS RECT 2 3 0 0
COBS RECTE 1 1.5 0.2 0.1
COBS TILTE 0.4
EOS
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 21
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 1
CLAP 1.5 0 0
CLAP ELIPE 1 3 0.1 0.2
CLAP TILTE 0.3
CHG 2
COBS RECT 2 3 0 0
COBS ELIPE 1 1.5 0.2 0.1
COBS TILTE 0.4
EOS
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 22
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 1
CLAP 1.5 0 0
CLAP RCTKE 1 3 0.1 0.2 0.5
CLAP TILTE 0.3
CHG 2
COBS RECT 2 3 0 0
COBS RCTKE 1.5 1 0.2 0.1 0.5
COBS TILTE 0.4
CHG 3
CLAP 1.5 0 0
CLAP RCTKE 3 1 0.1 0.2 0.5
CHG 4
CLAP 1.5 0 0
CLAP RCTKE 2 2 0.1 0.2 2
CHG 5
COBS RECT 2 3 0 0
COBS RCTKE 2 2 0.2 0.1 2
EOS
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 23
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 2
COBS RECT 2 3 0 0
COBS POLYE 1.5 6 0.2 0.1
COBS TILTE 0.4
EOS
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 24
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 1
CLAP 3 0 0
FOOTBLOK YES
CHG 2
CLAP 3 0 0
COBS 1 0 0
SPIDER 4 45 0.2
EOS
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 25
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 1
CLAP 3 0 0
MULTCLAP 1 0.5 0.3 10
MULTCLAP 2 -0.4 0.2 -5
MULTCLAP 3 0.2 -0.6 0
CHG 2
CLAP RECT 2 3 0 0
COBS 1 0.1 0.1
MULTCLAP 1 0.3 0 15
MULTCOBS 1 0.5 0.4 0
MULTCOBS 2 -0.6 0 0
CHG 4
CLAP ELIP 3 2 0 0
COBS RECT 1 1.5 0 0
MULTCOBS 1 0.5 0.4 20
MULTCOBS 2 -0.6 0.1 0
EOS
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
! HITSUR / hit_and_interact cases (26-35).  The "HITSUR: cases N, skipped K,
! mismatches M" line of EVERY ENGINETEST (cases 1-25 included: the osdtriplet is
! the plain refracting-sphere case) runs, for each surface NEWOBJ+1..NEWIMG that
! the port supports, 26 fixed incoming rays (near-axis, off-axis, steep rays that
! cause TIR at glass->air surfaces, near-grazing, backward-travelling rays) in
! that surface's frame x two signs of the starting z x wavelength slots 1-3 x four
! REVSTR/RV/RVSTART combinations x (on surface NEWOBJ+1) two distinct aim points,
! through legacy HITSUR and the port from identical sentinel state, and requires
! every value either leaves behind (ray, normal, COSI/COSIP, R_L0.., PHASE, TIR,
! RV, RVSTART, DUM, INTERS/SEC/OLDL.., STOPP, RAYCOD, SPDCD, HOE_DO_IT) to be
! identical bit for bit.  Unsupported surfaces are counted as "skipped" and the
! port must decline them without touching its state.  Beyond the fixture lenses,
! a synthetic pass declines each gate condition (special type, array parity,
! paraxial, grating, PERFECT, IDEAL, ray error, clap decenter 13, stale or
! missing typed surface, wavelength slot out of range) on a copy of the data.
!
!   case 26  even asphere surfaces (CV2PRG LithoKotaro.seq): the asphere_surface
!            intersect, refraction at many glass/air interfaces, 61 surfaces
!   case 27  mirror (negative index after the surface): the reflection branch
!            (SIGNNU < 0, reflection mode 0), sign flip of the index
!   case 28  reflection mode 1 (RMD S1 TIR = REFLTIRO): the "TIRTESTER > 1"
!            test.  TIRTESTER = SINI*SNINDX with SNINDX = +-1 and SINI <= 1, so
!            the legacy test is never true and RAYCOD 20 can never occur; the
!            port reproduces that (the case documents it: code 20 count is 0)
!   case 29  tilted mirror (STILT on the mirror surface; tilts are applied by
!            TRNSF2, not by HITSUR, so the in-frame results are unchanged)
!   case 30  dummy surface (INS + GLA with the same glass as the previous
!            surface: all 10 indices equal and DUMMMY true): the DUM = .TRUE.
!            path that skips the deflection but still does COSI/RV bookkeeping
!   case 31  mirror followed by negative thicknesses (reversed rays: RV true and
!            the TESTLEN / SNINDX / REVSTR / RVSTART combinations)
!   case 32  gated surfaces: CLAP x-decenter 13 (S2), RAYERROR (S3), IDEAL (S5)
!            and PERFECT (S6) are skipped.  No FOB, no grating, no PARAX here:
!            the chief ray of such a lens cannot be traced, and the grating and
!            paraxial commands make EOS print ray-failure messages; those two
!            gates are covered by the synthetic pass instead
!   case 33  stale typed-surface array (INS without a resync): the typed-path
!            guard fails, every surface is skipped
!   case 34  toric flag with special type 0 (YTORIC + RDTOR): HITSUR's typed path
!            never reads the toric flag, so the surface is intersected as the
!            rotationally symmetric sphere; both sides do the same
! TIR (RAYCOD 4) at glass->air surfaces occurs in every refractive case (see the
! DETAIL line of a non-BRIEF ENGINETEST).
! ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

! case 26
CV2PRG LithoKotaro.seq
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 27
LEN NEW
EPD 20
TIT 'OSDmirror'
RDY S1 -100
RMD S1 REFL
PIM
FOB 0
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 28
LEN NEW
EPD 20
TIT 'OSDmirror'
RDY S1 -100
RMD S1 TIR
PIM
FOB 0
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 29
LEN NEW
EPD 20
TIT 'OSDmirror'
RDY S1 -100
RMD S1 REFL
PIM
STILT 1 3 0 0
FOB 0
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 30
RES osdtriplet
INS S6
GLA S6 SK16
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 31
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 5
REFL
THI -4
CHG 6
THI -4
EOS
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 32
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 2
CLAP 3 0 13
CHG 3
RAYERROR 2
CHG 5
IDEAL 50
CHG 6
PERFECT
EOS
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 33
RES osdtriplet
INS S4
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 34
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 3
YTORIC
RDTOR 20
EOS
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
! Ray aiming leaf routines (cases 35-55).  The six lines after HITSUR in the
! output compare the legacy routines with their ports in mod_ray_aiming, bit for
! bit:
!   AIMTARGET  compute_aim_target (and APLANA): the target point on the
!              reference surface for a 13x13 grid of relative pupil coordinates
!              over [-1.2, 1.2]^2, for ANAAIM true and false
!   GETZEE1    the aim point -> surface 1 intersection, for a grid of aim points
!              and object points, for the lens as it stands and for synthetic
!              surface-1 curvatures/conics (flat, sphere, parabola (conic -1: one
!              intersection), oblate and prolate conics); points off the surface
!              reach the ZEEERR miss exit
!   RAYDERIV   the four derivatives for pairs incl. equal (zero) denominators
!   NEWDEL     one Newton step, for a derivative quadruple that takes each
!              branch, for several landing errors, aim points, object points and
!              the same surface-1 variants (so both with and without GETZEE1)
!   MISSREF    "is the reference-surface point blocked by the clear aperture"
!              over a grid and the nominal edges, REFMISS starting false and true
!   ADJLAST    adjustLastSurface on real RAYRAY data from legacy RAYTRA2 traces
!              of six rays, at every surface, for the real and synthetic
!              thicknesses (negative: reversed; huge: the 1e10 guard)
! Every ENGINETEST (cases 1-34 included) also runs synthetic passes that
! temporarily rewrite the reference surface's clear aperture (every type, centred
! or decentered/tilted), curvature and array parity, the aplanatic / flip /
! orientation settings, and surface 1's curvature and conic, then restore them,
! so branches that no command can set up on the current lens are covered anyway.
! The AIM SETUP line summarises what the case's own lens sets up.
!
! NEWDEL branches (legacy order; "NEWDEL DETAIL" of a non-BRIEF run counts the
! cases per branch, 72 each):
!   0 all derivatives zero (failure: RAYCOD 16, MACFAL due)   1 D11&D22
!   2 D11&D12   3 D21&D12   4 D21&D22   5 D11&D21   6 D12&D22   7 only D22
!   8 only D11   9 only D12   (10 = a copy of 7 that can never run: unreachable)
!   11 only D21: no branch matches, the routine returns having changed nothing
!
! Not reachable from commands, covered by the synthetic passes: IPOLY (type 6)
! reference apertures, array parity on the reference surface, a reference
! surface with MULTCLAP (REFS refuses one), the MISSREF types on a given lens.
! ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

! case 35: circular reference clap, centred, aplanatic off (osdtriplet reference
! surface = stop = S3)
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 3
CLAP 3.5 0 0
EOS
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 36: same, aplanatic aiming on: APLANA runs (|R| = 37.5 >= the radius)
RES osdtriplet
AIMAPL ON
U L
CHG 3
CLAP 3.5 0 0
EOS
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 37: circular clap with dim1 > dim2 (the smaller is the radius), aplanatic on
RES osdtriplet
AIMAPL ON
U L
CHG 3
CLAP 3.5 0 0 2.5
EOS
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 38: circular clap decentered: "clapt" branch, aplanatic skipped.  (CLAP TILT
! is refused for a circular clap, so a tilted circle only exists synthetically.)
RES osdtriplet
AIMAPL ON
U L
CHG 3
CLAP 3.5 0.2 -0.1
EOS
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 39: rectangular reference clap, centred
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 3
CLAP RECT 3.5 3.0 0 0
EOS
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 40: rectangular clap decentered and tilted (the ANAAIM branches of clapt)
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 3
CLAP RECT 3.5 3.0 0.2 -0.1
CLAP TILT 20
EOS
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 41: elliptical clap, centred
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 3
CLAP ELIP 3.5 3.0 0 0
EOS
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 42: elliptical clap decentered and tilted
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 3
CLAP ELIP 3.5 3.0 0.2 -0.1
CLAP TILT 25
EOS
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 43: racetrack clap (centred; the 8-sided box in MISSREF)
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 3
CLAP RCTK 3.5 3.0 0 0 1
EOS
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 44: polygon clap, decentered and tilted
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 3
CLAP POLY 3.5 6 0.1 -0.2
CLAP TILT 12
EOS
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 45: FLIPREFX on (no clap on the reference surface: paraxial target)
RES osdtriplet
FLIPREFX ON
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 46: FLIPREFY on with a rectangular clap
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 3
CLAP RECT 3.5 3.0 0 0
EOS
FLIPREFY ON
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 47: both flips with a decentered, tilted rectangular clap
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 3
CLAP RECT 3.5 3.0 0.2 -0.1
CLAP TILT 20
EOS
FLIPREFX ON
FLIPREFY ON
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 48: reference surface orientation 30 degrees with an elliptical clap
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 3
CLAP ELIP 3.5 3.0 0 0
REFS 30
EOS
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 49: reference surface orientation with no clap (paraxial target rotated)
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 3
REFS 30
EOS
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 50: ray aiming off (osdtriplet has it on by default, as in every other
! case; AIMAPL ON in 36-38 turns it off in favour of aplanatic aiming)
RES osdtriplet
AIMRAY OFF
U L
CHG 3
CLAP 3.5 0 0
EOS
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 51: surface 1 flat (GETZEE1 guard: NEWDEL does not call it)
RES osdtriplet
RDY S1 0
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 52: surface 1 parabolic (conic -1): GETZEE1's single-intersection branch
RES osdtriplet
K S1 -1
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 53: surface 1 oblate conic with a tilt and decenter (BAKONE/FORONEL in
! GETZEE1 and NEWDEL on a placed surface 1)
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 1
K 0.5
TILT 0.5 0.3 0.2
DEC 0.1 -0.2 0.3
EOS
FOB 0.7
ENGINETEST BRIEF

! case 54: last surface with a positive thickness (adjustLastSurface does work)
